WEBVTT

00:12.970 --> 00:18.710
Hikari ga sasu sora, umareochiru kage
In the bright sky illuminated by
sunlight, darkened shadows are born.

00:18.810 --> 00:24.150
Unmei wa dokomademo hikisakareru
Fate itself is being torn apart.

00:25.190 --> 00:30.150
Donna toki mo kesshite akiramenainara
If you never give up, no matter what happens,

00:30.330 --> 00:37.560
mada tozasareteru tobira kanarazu hiraku
Even that locked door will open for you.

00:38.530 --> 00:43.990
Eien datte dakishimete, fuuin mo tokihanachi
Embrace eternity and release the seal.

00:44.070 --> 00:49.940
Mamorubekimono ga ima kokoni wa arukara
Because the ones you wish
to protect are right here.

00:49.940 --> 00:55.880
Namida mo gyutto dakishimete,
yasashisa de tsutsumikomi
Embrace their tears with kindness.

00:55.880 --> 01:01.560
Nagareru mizu no youni tsuyoku nare
Become strong like the formless water,

01:01.560 --> 01:07.550
omouyouni tsuyoku nare
Become as strong as you wish to be.

01:07.700 --> 01:13.170
Mou jibun ni obienaide
Stop being afraid of yourself.

01:13.170 --> 01:19.800
Sou mirai wo osorenaide
Do not fear the future.

01:43.430 --> 01:47.800
High school girls can even lose these?

01:48.370 --> 01:49.630
They can be so careless.

02:19.900 --> 02:21.390
Wh-Who's there?!

02:46.230 --> 02:51.160
Our Fox Deity, Conducts a Treatment

02:52.270 --> 02:54.060
H-Hold on!

02:54.340 --> 02:55.640
K-Ko!

02:55.640 --> 02:58.270
Are your hands shaking?

02:58.270 --> 02:59.210
No.

02:59.670 --> 03:03.130
Yes, they are! They're really shaking!

03:04.050 --> 03:05.680
They are not shaking.

03:05.680 --> 03:06.880
It will be all right.

03:06.880 --> 03:10.080
It's not okay! That's enough! You can't do it!

03:10.080 --> 03:12.350
Noboru-sama, stop moving.

03:13.520 --> 03:14.590
Stop!

03:14.590 --> 03:15.350
Toru-sama.

03:16.220 --> 03:17.250
Yeah?

03:17.660 --> 03:20.130
I will finish with him soon, so please wait here.

03:32.370 --> 03:34.600
A gray werewolf?

03:34.780 --> 03:35.540
What's that?

03:35.980 --> 03:38.000
Everyone's talking about it!

03:38.450 --> 03:43.180
Weird things have been happening around
Akagi for the last three weeks or so.

03:44.350 --> 03:49.120
Mr. A was walking along the riverbank
on his way home from cram school.

03:49.620 --> 03:54.320
He saw a woman by the river and
called out to her without thinking.

03:54.630 --> 03:57.720
"Be careful! It's dangerous over there," he said.

03:58.600 --> 04:01.260
"What? I can't hear you."

04:01.440 --> 04:05.200
The woman kept repeating that over and
over again as she walked up to Mr. A.

04:05.570 --> 04:08.840
And when he saw her face...

04:18.790 --> 04:19.850
That's what happened.

04:19.850 --> 04:24.150
Scary, right? It's our city's
very own urban legend!

04:25.560 --> 04:27.560
I thought you'd be more freaked out.

04:27.560 --> 04:29.150
I am.

04:29.530 --> 04:32.520
You know the guy with the
nickname Pakeratta in Class 1?

04:32.670 --> 04:34.070
He lives in Akagi.

04:34.770 --> 04:37.140
Pakeratta? You mean THAT Pakeratta?

04:37.340 --> 04:39.170
Yeah, the guy from Hashimoto Barbershop.

04:39.610 --> 04:43.070
He's been absent from school
for about a week now.

04:43.480 --> 04:47.820
I hear it's because he was bitten
on the neck by that gray werewolf!

04:47.820 --> 04:52.050
The bite mark is completely swollen
and his fever won't come down!

04:53.090 --> 04:54.650
Scary, right?!

04:55.160 --> 04:58.390
It's not as unbelievable as other urban legends.

04:58.390 --> 05:00.760
It feels real since it happened
to someone we know.

05:03.100 --> 05:05.220
So it's not just a rumor.

05:09.070 --> 05:12.770
This is the crepe store that appears
randomly around the park!

05:12.770 --> 05:15.140
Don't the crepes look really good?!

05:15.740 --> 05:16.870
Yeah...

05:21.720 --> 05:23.950
Hey, what happened to your ear?

05:24.120 --> 05:27.990
Just experiencing first hand that when
something sounds too good to be true...

05:27.990 --> 05:28.850
...it probably is.

05:30.730 --> 05:32.060
Okay, whatever.

05:32.060 --> 05:36.190
By the way, the teachers were talking up
a storm in the office.

05:36.360 --> 05:37.730
About what?

05:38.070 --> 05:44.630
It was something about seeing
a red fox in the hallways this morning.

05:45.610 --> 05:47.630
You know something about it?

05:47.780 --> 05:49.980
N-Nah.

05:49.980 --> 05:51.040
Midori-kun!

05:55.750 --> 05:57.220
Hi, Momiji.

05:59.290 --> 06:02.650
I didn't know they were on a first name basis.

06:03.060 --> 06:05.390
Here's what I was talking
to you about, Midori-kun.

06:05.730 --> 06:06.730
Oh, thanks.

06:06.730 --> 06:07.560
What's that?

06:07.630 --> 06:12.400
Well, I'm going to hold a mini-concert
at my home this Christmas.

06:12.870 --> 06:15.560
And I got invited.

06:15.770 --> 06:17.470
Momiji is going to be performing solo.

06:18.870 --> 06:21.580
Well, Miyabe-san is really good at singing.

06:21.580 --> 06:23.110
Like during the Culture Festival.

06:23.110 --> 06:26.550
Thank you! But it feels kind of embarrassing now.

06:27.520 --> 06:29.570
I know. Why don't you come, Takagami?

06:30.080 --> 06:31.820
That would be great if you could!

06:31.820 --> 06:35.410
I still have plenty of tickets
so I'll get you one tomorrow. How about it?

06:35.660 --> 06:37.530
Uh, sure.

06:37.530 --> 06:40.360
Hey, Noboru-kun. What happened to your ear?

06:41.000 --> 06:44.360
He said that if something sounds
too good to be true, it usually is.

06:44.600 --> 06:46.930
What's that supposed to mean?

06:46.930 --> 06:49.900
It's nothing. I was just messing with him.

06:50.100 --> 06:52.370
It looks like it hurts. Are you okay?

06:54.910 --> 06:56.600
Y-Yeah...

07:05.190 --> 07:07.120
Bye. I need to go back.

07:09.720 --> 07:11.780
Don't give up, Sakura Misaki!

07:26.210 --> 07:29.900
Maybe I should take the
first step and ask him out.

07:32.180 --> 07:33.700
I can't!

07:33.880 --> 07:36.780
He'll definitely turn me down!

07:36.950 --> 07:39.040
Looks like something's bothering you.

07:41.860 --> 07:43.920
It's probably about Noboru, isn't it?

07:44.160 --> 07:45.020
Tenko-san!

07:47.730 --> 07:51.160
The red fox they saw was probably...

07:52.700 --> 07:54.190
Yeah...

07:55.800 --> 07:57.170
Ogami-san!

08:01.910 --> 08:06.050
How could he put you in so much agony?

08:06.050 --> 08:10.180
I don't believe that blockhead.

08:10.380 --> 08:12.680
All right. Let me help you.

08:13.350 --> 08:14.720
B-But...

08:14.860 --> 08:17.480
It's like helping the enemy in her case!

08:17.590 --> 08:20.860
Just leave it to me. I knew
something like this would happen...

08:21.200 --> 08:22.320
Tadah!

08:22.500 --> 08:25.690
Here's a potion to make Noboru
notice everything good about you!

08:27.170 --> 08:29.030
Th-That can't be real...

08:29.340 --> 08:31.100
Sakura, take a swig of this.

08:31.670 --> 08:34.140
Then get Noboru to drink the rest.

08:34.240 --> 08:38.470
It'll be an indirect kiss, but don't worry about it.

08:38.810 --> 08:42.040
I-Indirect...

08:43.250 --> 08:44.880
Come on! Drink!

08:57.060 --> 08:59.090
This tastes terrible.

08:59.330 --> 09:01.370
Medicine has to be bitter!

09:01.370 --> 09:03.600
Now make sure you get Noboru to drink the rest.

09:09.140 --> 09:11.200
All right. I'll try.

09:11.350 --> 09:13.480
Okay. Good luck!

09:13.480 --> 09:15.070
Thanks! I'll try my best!

09:17.790 --> 09:20.310
Yes, because I'll need you to...

09:35.370 --> 09:36.500
Here I go!

09:36.970 --> 09:38.270
Take that!

09:41.580 --> 09:45.100
You saw a wolf yokai while
you were making your rounds?

09:45.650 --> 09:47.410
Did he look dangerous?

09:47.950 --> 09:51.820
He looked like he was hungry for something.

09:52.850 --> 09:54.880
Hungry...

09:55.820 --> 09:56.690
Takagami.

09:58.330 --> 10:00.350
Seems like you're not in top condition today.

10:00.800 --> 10:02.560
I just had some stuff happen.

10:04.200 --> 10:05.960
I can't concentrate on my badminton game...

10:06.370 --> 10:08.960
What? Is something bothering you?

10:12.070 --> 10:15.700
You're the only one who
worries about me like this.

10:16.540 --> 10:18.170
You were kidding?

10:18.510 --> 10:20.100
I can never tell...

10:20.750 --> 10:23.410
Anyway, Takagami...

10:24.790 --> 10:26.490
I want you to drink this.

10:26.490 --> 10:27.680
What's that?

10:28.360 --> 10:30.630
Uh, this is...

10:30.630 --> 10:33.360
My own special energy drink recipe!

10:34.760 --> 10:36.000
You sure you want me to have it?

10:36.000 --> 10:37.330
Yeah! Go right ahead!

10:38.030 --> 10:39.530
Wait, right now?

10:39.530 --> 10:40.830
Of course...

10:41.070 --> 10:42.590
Well, um...

10:43.070 --> 10:45.910
I'm not that thirsty right now...

10:45.910 --> 10:49.100
Oh, really. I guess you wouldn't be...

10:52.910 --> 10:54.510
But I want you to drink it right now!

10:55.280 --> 10:56.080
Please!

10:56.620 --> 10:58.350
Why does Takagami get to have all the fun?

10:59.450 --> 11:00.920
I want some, too.

11:01.790 --> 11:03.760
No!

11:08.860 --> 11:10.130
Takagami, please!

11:11.430 --> 11:13.230
Drink up!

11:13.670 --> 11:14.500
Sure...

11:26.850 --> 11:30.550
It might taste a little bad, but it really works!

11:30.550 --> 11:31.620
Oh, really.

11:31.620 --> 11:33.140
Thanks, Sakura.

11:33.350 --> 11:34.320
Yeah!

11:38.290 --> 11:43.000
That's what they said. Have you
ever heard of the gray werewolf?

11:43.000 --> 11:43.760
No.

11:43.860 --> 11:46.500
That's pretty similar to what Ogami-san said.

11:46.500 --> 11:48.300
Did something happen to Ogami-san?

11:48.470 --> 11:52.670
He was making his nightly rounds and
came across some wolf monster in a classroom.

11:52.670 --> 11:55.310
Then it growled at him or something.

11:55.310 --> 11:56.470
R-Really?!

11:56.610 --> 12:03.210
Don't worry. If that thing ever attacks you,
I'll tear it apart.

12:23.240 --> 12:24.800
Too bad.

12:24.970 --> 12:27.300
Another fake.

12:30.210 --> 12:34.080
Seeing as how fakes are
sent out night after night...

12:36.220 --> 12:40.180
The host of this infection
must be really prudent...

12:56.940 --> 12:59.200
Here's the ticket I promised you yesterday.

12:59.310 --> 13:00.640
Thanks.

13:01.040 --> 13:05.570
Sorry for bothering you during practice,
but I really wanted to see you.

13:07.380 --> 13:08.310
Just kidding!

13:11.790 --> 13:12.950
Sorry.

13:13.150 --> 13:15.950
Anyway, will you be able to come on the 24th?

13:16.060 --> 13:17.630
Yeah, it won't be a problem.

13:17.630 --> 13:20.990
That's great! It'll make preparing
for the party that much more fun!

13:21.800 --> 13:22.990
I'll be looking forward to it.

13:23.200 --> 13:25.320
But isn't preparing everything a lot of work?

13:25.570 --> 13:28.830
Not really. It's not so bad
I can't do it on my own.

13:28.970 --> 13:31.060
I ordered catering for the food and...

13:31.210 --> 13:33.440
Wait, you're doing it alone?

13:35.880 --> 13:38.340
I'm the only one at home right now.

13:38.680 --> 13:41.770
My father is always overseas
and I don't have a mother.

13:43.550 --> 13:48.220
We're a motherless family. I've been living
alone for as long as I can remember.

13:51.560 --> 13:52.750
Me, too.

13:54.090 --> 13:55.650
My dad's a single father, too.

13:55.830 --> 13:57.300
I don't have a mother.

13:59.500 --> 14:00.630
Oh...

14:02.240 --> 14:05.100
I guess we're the same.

14:06.310 --> 14:09.380
It feels like we're connected in some way!

14:09.380 --> 14:11.000
Well, I'll see you then!

14:11.350 --> 14:12.370
Sure thing.

14:17.420 --> 14:18.320
Takagami.

14:19.250 --> 14:20.520
Let's walk home together today!

14:20.690 --> 14:21.710
Uh, sure.

14:23.320 --> 14:25.990
It's nice for you guys to come visit!

14:25.990 --> 14:28.860
This crepe store is really good, you know!

14:29.030 --> 14:34.160
The store is in a van so sometimes
it's hard to find! We're in luck today!

14:34.370 --> 14:36.200
What is a crepe?

14:36.200 --> 14:39.710
It's a Western dessert.
Is this the first time you had one?

14:39.710 --> 14:40.370
Yes.

14:40.540 --> 14:43.100
Then let's start with the basics.

14:44.750 --> 14:45.970
Excuse me!

14:46.280 --> 14:47.680
Yes?

14:50.150 --> 14:51.710
Welcome.

14:54.860 --> 14:58.460
Can you come to the chem lab with me?

14:58.460 --> 14:59.480
Why?

14:59.760 --> 15:01.790
You know how I'm on duty today?

15:01.960 --> 15:06.920
During 5th period, they told me I had to take
everyone's notebooks to the teacher's office.

15:07.070 --> 15:09.700
But I don't think I can carry them all by myself.

15:10.070 --> 15:12.740
Oh, okay. Sure, I'll go with you.

15:12.740 --> 15:14.900
Thanks! Now, let's go.

15:17.340 --> 15:22.610
Some dangerous gray things are
wandering around this area recently.

15:22.880 --> 15:24.010
The werewolves?

15:24.390 --> 15:27.010
That's right. You know about them?

15:27.150 --> 15:28.750
People were talking about it at school.

15:31.560 --> 15:34.030
About those gray werewolves...

15:34.300 --> 15:37.360
My yokai said they haven't seen them.

15:37.870 --> 15:42.170
The Hashihime should be on the lookout
for drifting yokai that come into my land...

15:42.400 --> 15:44.460
Maybe she just missed them.

15:44.840 --> 15:49.430
That's what I thought at first. But the
more I looked into it, the less I could find.

15:49.710 --> 15:51.300
That was good!

15:51.750 --> 15:54.920
There's something I have to do now.
Thanks for the food.

15:54.920 --> 15:56.720
Hey, were you listening?

15:56.720 --> 15:59.190
You have to protect Toru-chan!

16:01.090 --> 16:06.390
Tenko-sama has been going somewhere
at this hour for the past few days.

16:07.430 --> 16:09.230
I wonder where she's going.

16:10.700 --> 16:14.230
Seems like those three couldn't tell it was me.

16:16.170 --> 16:18.910
Well, I'll be counting on you.

16:18.910 --> 16:20.310
And the same to you.

16:33.950 --> 16:37.480
Let's see. Where do they
usually leave the notebooks?

16:38.090 --> 16:38.850
Over here?

16:42.560 --> 16:44.120
Wh-What was that?!

16:47.600 --> 16:51.270
B-Bring T-Takagami.

16:51.270 --> 16:52.670
H-Hashimoto?

16:52.840 --> 16:55.810
T-Takagami...

16:57.280 --> 16:58.400
H-Hey!

16:59.110 --> 17:01.600
Infect Takagami!

17:04.350 --> 17:06.050
Sorry I'm late!

17:08.360 --> 17:09.320
Takagami...

17:10.320 --> 17:12.660
No way! Did he leave without me again?

17:16.000 --> 17:18.330
Or did he go with Miyabe-san?

17:43.920 --> 17:46.120
Hashimoto, what happened to...

17:46.290 --> 17:51.250
I-I-Infect T-Ta-Takagami.

17:51.570 --> 17:54.760
Infect Takagami!

18:07.010 --> 18:08.170
Sakura?

18:20.390 --> 18:21.190
Sakura!

18:30.870 --> 18:32.600
No way...

18:42.280 --> 18:43.940
S-Sakura-san...

18:44.220 --> 18:45.010
Don't tell me you're...

18:45.150 --> 18:48.350
We're on the 3rd floor!

18:56.100 --> 18:56.890
There you are.

18:59.230 --> 19:00.030
Ku?

19:06.710 --> 19:07.800
Good work.

19:07.910 --> 19:10.970
What are you talking about?!
What's going on here?!

19:11.150 --> 19:14.980
Things were getting dangerous around you.

19:14.980 --> 19:18.850
I hypnotized Sakura as a precaution for you.

19:19.150 --> 19:20.180
Hypnotized?

19:20.620 --> 19:26.150
I ordered her to protect you at
all costs if you were put in danger.

19:26.260 --> 19:27.860
Why did it have to be Sakura?!

19:27.860 --> 19:30.160
Why would you make her do
something so dangerous?!

19:30.400 --> 19:33.560
That's because you wouldn't
let me in the school and...

19:36.040 --> 19:37.630
That was fast.

19:39.240 --> 19:40.210
K-Ku...

19:40.370 --> 19:41.270
Don't worry.

19:49.680 --> 19:50.780
What did you?

19:51.820 --> 19:53.950
What is that? What did you do to him?

19:53.950 --> 19:57.720
This? It's some thing they call a "vaccine."

19:57.720 --> 19:59.250
Vaccine? For what?

19:59.660 --> 20:02.560
For a dangerous kind of rabies.

20:03.300 --> 20:04.990
What's going on here?

20:05.330 --> 20:07.130
He's one of the infected.

20:07.470 --> 20:09.590
To be brief, they're, uh...

20:10.140 --> 20:15.140
"When bitten by the host,
they are given a variety of powers..."

20:15.140 --> 20:20.310
"...but they also fall completely
under the host's control."

20:20.450 --> 20:21.570
That's what it says.

20:22.750 --> 20:24.410
The gray werewolf!

20:33.490 --> 20:34.220
Hey...

20:34.390 --> 20:35.760
Are you awake?

20:36.700 --> 20:38.000
T-Takagami?!

20:38.000 --> 20:39.430
What happened to me?!

20:39.700 --> 20:43.540
Don't you remember?
You passed out in the middle of the street.

20:43.540 --> 20:46.060
You're kidding. I don't remember that at all.

20:46.770 --> 20:48.670
Um, Takagami...

20:49.810 --> 20:52.450
Well, aren't I heavy?

20:52.450 --> 20:54.110
I'm sorry about this...

20:54.380 --> 20:55.780
Don't worry about it.

20:55.780 --> 20:58.620
Besides, we promised we'd walk home together.

20:58.990 --> 21:00.850
I'll walk you back home.

21:02.660 --> 21:04.930
This isn't fair.

21:04.930 --> 21:07.450
When I see you like this...

21:08.060 --> 21:10.930
Thank you, Takagami.

21:38.190 --> 21:43.420
Hare mo ke mo naku oowarawa de neboketerarenai
With all the commotion, I can't stay still.

21:43.960 --> 21:49.490
Kidoairaku gochamaze aa ijou
With emotions running wild,
everything seems so odd.

21:49.800 --> 21:55.300
Inochimijikashi toiunonara hara wo kukutte
Life is short so be prepared for anything.

21:55.580 --> 22:00.710
Iran kyoukai nanno sono yuke
Transcend that useless boundary and go!

22:00.780 --> 22:01.410
Kitsune Soba

22:01.780 --> 22:07.410
kingin kagayaku suteki na mainichi
With those bright days behind you,

22:07.590 --> 22:13.360
omatsurisawagi de mairouka
It's time for some merrymaking.

22:13.960 --> 22:19.760
Sora ni hi wo tomoshi tamashii no pareedo
Light the skies for this parade of souls,

22:19.930 --> 22:25.630
shiawase no kotodama hora kousa suru
The kotodama of happiness crosses paths.

22:25.810 --> 22:31.370
Namida mo wasurete odori odore
Forget those tears and dance away,

22:31.610 --> 22:37.550
toriaezu iiyone tanoshikeryasa
Forget about everything else
since we're having fun now.

22:50.460 --> 22:52.260
You don't know how lucky you are.

22:52.670 --> 23:01.230
That spell only works on someone who is always
watching Noboru and also deeply cares for him.

23:02.140 --> 23:07.170
I don't know who it is,
but I'll make you regret attacking Noboru.

23:10.580 --> 23:12.420
What was I doing?

23:13.490 --> 23:15.350
Plan B failed, too.

23:15.660 --> 23:16.850
Oh, well.

23:17.120 --> 23:19.320
I made a Plan C for this situation.

23:19.690 --> 23:22.920
Just you wait. I will make you mine.

23:25.000 --> 23:26.000
Next Time

23:26.000 --> 23:28.140
Next Time
It's time for Miyabe-san's Christmas party!

23:28.140 --> 23:28.240
Next Time

23:28.240 --> 23:30.900
Next Time
But a mysterious flying fish
appeared before my eyes!

23:30.900 --> 23:33.370
Next Time
He says he's a servant of the Miyabe family...

23:33.370 --> 23:33.440
Next Time

23:33.440 --> 23:35.180
Next Time
Next time, "Our Fox Deity, Crashes a Party."

23:35.180 --> 23:36.210
Next Time
Our Fox Deity, Crashes a Party
Next time, "Our Fox Deity, Crashes a Party."

23:36.210 --> 23:38.880
Next Time
Our Fox Deity, Crashes a Party
Sugarcoated words are never
what they seem! I think...

23:38.880 --> 23:39.940
Next Time
Our Fox Deity, Crashes a Party
